Given an integer array nums of size n. Return the maximum sum possible using the elements of nums such that no two
elements taken are adjacent in nums.

Example 1:
Input: nums = [1, 2, 4]
Output: 5
Explanation:
[1, 2, 4], the underlined elements are taken to get the maximum sum.

Example 2:
Input: nums = [2, 1, 4, 9]
Output: 11
Explanation:
[2, 1, 4, 9], the underlined elements are taken to get the maximum sum.

Approach:
Use the pick and not pick recursive technique and then optimise it through DP.

Naive approach -> TC = O(2^n), SC = O(n)
Memoization -> TC = O(n), SC = O(n) + O(n) (recursion stack space)
Tabulation -> TC = O(n), SC = O(n)
Tabulation_SpaceOptimisation -> TC = O(n), SC = O(1)